cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "OES-512 Telemetry Engine: synthetic 512-channel framing, filtering and summary statistics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brisson
    given-names: Jean-François
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/oes512-telemetry-engine"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  A small asynchronous Python prototype that frames, filters and summarizes
  synthetic 512-channel telemetry: binary frames with a header, sequence ID,
  timestamp and checksum; a stateful 50 Hz notch and 0.5-45 Hz Butterworth
  bandpass per channel; and rolling-window statistics. The statistics are
  plain definitions: 'coherence' is the mean absolute Pearson correlation over
  32 sampled channels, 'instability' is the standard deviation of per-channel
  variances, and 'drift' is the distance of the per-channel mean from the
  first full window. Threshold alerts go to a local log; webhook POSTs are
  opt-in. Scope: all input comes from a deterministic built-in generator with
  a synthetic step disturbance. It is not acquisition hardware, has no
  connection to real sensors, and no latency or throughput has been measured;
  alert thresholds are uncalibrated defaults.
keywords:
  - research software
  - telemetry
  - digital signal processing
  - SciPy
  - asyncio
